<ContentLayout
  title="Comprehensive Website Audit: Scope and Deliverables"
  description="See what a comprehensive website audit can cover, which evidence and deliverables to agree, and when AuditWeb's $997 USD scope or a custom quote fits."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} toc={toc} publishDate="2026-03-28" updateDate="2026-09-11" showLeadForm={true}
>
<p>A comprehensive website audit reviews several connected systems against a written business question. AuditWeb's service can combine technical SEO, content, performance, user journeys and authorised public security observations.</p>
<p>The comprehensive service starts at $997 USD. Confirm the page and template sample, data access, deliverables, timing and exclusions before work begins.</p>

<h2 id="what-comprehensive-means">What makes a website audit comprehensive?</h2>
<p>A comprehensive audit connects evidence across agreed review areas. It does not claim that one fixed checklist can test every page, legal duty, security risk or user need.</p>
<p>The scope should name the website properties, priority journeys, important templates, measurement period and questions. Large sites use samples and system-level checks that the report must document.</p>

<h2 id="the-72-checkpoints">Which areas can the audit review?</h2>
<p>The audit can review seven practical areas. The exact checks depend on available evidence and the systems included in the quote.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Search access:</strong> response codes, robots rules, sitemaps, canonicals and internal discovery.</li>
  <li><strong>On-page content:</strong> titles, descriptions, headings, intent, duplication and internal links.</li>
  <li><strong>Rendering and architecture:</strong> templates, navigation, JavaScript output and URL patterns.</li>
  <li><strong>Performance:</strong> LCP, INP and CLS evidence with field or lab source stated.</li>
  <li><strong>User journeys:</strong> mobile layouts, navigation, forms and agreed conversion paths.</li>
  <li><strong>Accessibility observations:</strong> selected automated and manual checks. This is not a compliance certification.</li>
  <li><strong>Security observations:</strong> agreed public HTTPS and header checks. Active tests require explicit authorisation.</li>
</ul>
<p>Google documents LCP, INP and CLS in its <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/core-web-vitals">Core Web Vitals guidance</a>. The report should state the evidence type rather than mixing a Lighthouse lab run with field data.</p>

<h2 id="what-you-get">What does the comprehensive audit deliver?</h2>
<p>The standard deliverable is a prioritised report. Each finding records the affected URL or template, dated evidence, consequence, recommended change and verification step.</p>
<p>Agree any executive summary, implementation tracker, exports, presentation or walkthrough in the quote. View the <a href="/website-audit-services/report-example/">website audit report example</a> and <a href="/resources/agency-audit-toolkit/">editable toolkit</a> before choosing the format.</p>

<h2 id="timeline">How long does a comprehensive audit take?</h2>
<p>Timing depends on site size, template variety, access, sample depth and manual testing. AuditWeb confirms a delivery date after reviewing the scope.</p>
<p>The plan should leave time to validate tool findings and write verification criteria. An instant tool export is a different product from a manually reviewed audit.</p>

<h2 id="who-it-is-for">Who should choose the comprehensive scope?</h2>
<p>Choose a comprehensive audit when one decision spans several site systems. Suitable triggers include a redesign, migration, unexplained decline, major template release or backlog that needs independent prioritisation.</p>
<p>Choose the $297 basic scope when the problem and page sample are narrow. Choose a custom quote when the site is large, multilingual, multi-domain or technically unusual.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">How much does the comprehensive audit cost?</h2>
<p>The comprehensive AuditWeb audit starts at $997 USD. The final quote depends on pages, templates, data sources, review areas and deliverables.</p>
<p>Implementation and ongoing monitoring are separate unless stated in writing. Read the <a href="/website-audit-services/cost/">website audit cost guide</a> for a scope-based comparison.</p>

<h2 id="guarantee">Which terms and limits should the buyer confirm?</h2>
<p>Confirm the scope, price, delivery date, access, cancellation terms and follow-up support before work begins. AuditWeb does not guarantee a minimum finding count, rankings, traffic or revenue.</p>
<p>The report is evidence for decisions at the stated date. Re-test implemented changes and monitor outcomes with the same definitions before attributing a result to the audit.</p>
</ContentLayout>
